Well I decided to catch up here, and read all these polypile comments.

Note this response contains the necessary spoilers:


First I'd like to say that there are definate reasons for using a wand
of polymorph in NetHack.  Absolutely 100% valid reasons.  And any change
that I'd favor about the game (not that I'm the one who does such things)
should not hinder those reasons, because IMHO that would unbalance things.

Also, it was also suggested the "jealousy" was the reason that people like
myself were in favor of changing the behaviour of WoPs.  I do not think that
this is true.

If I really felt the desire to beat a fellow gamer's score, I
could spend as much time and effort as necessary to do so, and I'd use
every trick at my disposal to do so.  I'd have no qualm about it.  However,
in future revisions of the game, there are current behaviours that I'd
prefer to see changed.  The reason for that is to make the game (again IMHO)
more challenging for the players, because the game is currently to easy
to "abuse".  The change is being discussed and suggested because I think
the current WoP behaviour is unbalancing to the game, not because of
jealousy over any score.

The ultimate adjudicator of all play is the current code set (ie the game
itself).  Any score achievable in normal game play (ie not editing save files
or hacking binaries) is something to be admired, and is not supposed
to spark jealousy due to the methods used to gain that score.  However
the way to change these things (if one feels that they do not behave
properly) is to influence the future state of the code.  It's no jealousy
that drives this, it's just viewpoint.

Suggested changes have been:

1) Add a different scoreboard for polypilers.
Response) Get real.

2) Limit polypile & prompt player for specific item to poly object into.
Response) I do not like this because it makes the wand too much like wishing
Response) and it does not solve the problem that I find with the current
Response) polypile availabilty.  It still gives the player too much control
Response) over the outcome of the polymorph of objects.

3) Add chance for % destruction upon polymorph.
4) Add chance for % resistance upon polymorph.
Response) These two kind of go together.  I'd almost support this change
Response) but it has it's drawbacks too.  If a player *really does* need
Response) polymorph something (ie create dragon scale mail, or escape a
Response) nasty) I don't think that the ability of the wand to perform
Response) it's function should be denied to the player on random chance.
Response) I mean if you spent the time to kill the dragon, and make sure
Response) that you have a WoP handy, you *should* be rewarded with your
Response) scale mail, and not be denied over 5 zaps because of a quirk
Response) of fate.  It might be a while before you get to that point again!

5) Adjust final score based upon game duration.
Response) This is difficult since there are also valid situations where the
Response) game just goes longer.  If you remember this discussion started
Response) in an article where I had needed to spend an inordinate amount
Response) of time on levels 1-26 because I was unable to pass the Medusa
Response) because the game failed to generate a blindfold for me.

6) Disperse (ie teleport) objects upon polymorph.
Response) Amusing, and certainly a possible approach (maybe teleport all but
Response) the top item :-) but it gives the wand an extra non-intuitive
Response) ability that I do not think should be added.

On a side note: A suggestion that was made during this discussion to add
additional armor types to those that are available from polying corpses.
I really liked this suggestion, and it gets my vote (for what that's worth).
Also, the re-creation of golems (a la wand of undead turning on corpses)
on the piles left behind by them was very amusing, but would probably
be difficult to implement in the game.

